\contentsline {replaced}{Replaced: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{either a \emph {stub} $\mathsf {Mod}(q)$, or a \emph {full} reference $\mathsf {Mod}(q, \Gamma )$, which also carries the member context $\Gamma $ of $q$\ }}{2}{section*.1}%
\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{The \emph {dependencies} $\mathrm {deps}(q)$ of a module $q$ (Figure\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:modules}) are the modules its import prefix imports, together with their parents. Since imports precede statements, when a PurePy\xspace program runs under Python, every module in $\mathrm {deps}(q)$ is loaded before any statement of $q$ runs.}}{6}{section*.11}%
\contentsline {replaced}{Replaced: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{The output context $\Gamma $ of the module judgement comprises\ }}{10}{section*.19}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{and a stub for each submodule}}{10}{section*.20}%
\contentsline {replaced}{Replaced: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{The stubs and the module's own bindings are disjoint\ }}{10}{section*.21}%
\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Rule \textcolor {gray}{\textnormal {\textsf {qualified-submodule}}} requires the submodule to be among the dependencies $\mathrm {deps}(q_0)$ of the referring module $q_0$, ensuring it is loaded wherever the reference can be evaluated (Figure\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:prevented-errors}).}}{10}{section*.22}%
\contentsline {replaced}{Replaced: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{unless the module also imports \mbox {\lstinline [style=base16python]{a.b}}\ }}{19}{section*.25}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Extend (Definition\nobreakspace {}\ref {def:extend}) applies to module values as well: its equations are read with a loaded reference $\mathsf {Mod}(q, \rho )$ in place of a full reference and environments in place of contexts.}}{20}{section*.29}%
\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Loading is deterministic, so the metafunction $\mathrm {env}(q)$, the unique $\rho $ such that $q \Rightarrow _{\mathsf {load}} \rho $, is well-defined (Figure\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:eval-expr}).}}{20}{section*.30}%
\contentsline {replaced}{Replaced: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Loading mirrors the static structure: if $\vdash _{\mathcal {M}} q : \Gamma $ and $q \Rightarrow _{\mathsf {load}} \rho $ then $\vdash \rho : \Gamma $ (Figure\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:well-formed-env}).\ }}{20}{section*.31}%
